{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face","id":659038,"title":"For Evil Wears a Pleasant Face...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-10T00:39:49-07:00","id":659038,"title":"For Evil Wears a Pleasant Face...","content":"Spirits. We all know that, from a human perspective, they're pretty much universally evil. Part of what makes the World of Darkness so crapsack is that even spirits of pleasant places or positive concepts can be inhumanly cruel or destructive, since all they care about is promoting themselves and scoring more sweet, sweet Essence.<br /> <br /> Now, this is a wonderful bit of flavor and all, and really evocative... the thing is, it's not always easy to envision. I don't know, maybe it's just me, but has anyone else had problems envisioning how to pervert a kindergarten spirit or a joy spirit into something evil and inhuman?<br /> <br /> So, what I was hoping to do was to open this topic and give people a place to swap ideas, or experiences, with making villains or terrifying encounters out of &quot;good spirits&quot;. I hope folks are willing to share.<br /> <br /> Also, really need advice on making an evil figure out of a Joy spirit. Need it for an upcoming project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T01:48:54-07:00","id":659110,"title":"","content":"The Joker.<br /> <br /> But spirits aren't &quot;evil&quot;. They're amoral, and alien, but ultimately they they can be reasoned with. It would be difficult to justify the Forsaken taking totems otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 09-10-2015, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T02:24:11-07:00","id":659152,"title":"","content":"Ah ! Joy spirits ! They were the topic of the last game I ran with my werewolf group !<br /> <br /> Take a nursery, full of joy spirits : it's an heaven in the Shadows. But closed it, and soon the spirits will starve. Some of them cross to the Flesh, and bring children to play inside the ruined nursery, giving them a spark of joy to survive. But then a promotor want to build another building on it, and the Spirit kill him to protect its home. But the murder draw attention, so he must kill again, and the children come less and less. And the murders, with fear and violence, change the spirit, making it a terrifying maggath between Joy and Murder. And escalate more, given that it as anchored himself to a young child, it has now nearly claimed her.<br /> <br /> What will you do in this case, little wolf ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","user":"Arabidopsis","date":". 09-10-2015, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T03:27:16-07:00","id":659184,"title":"","content":"I think this exact example is in Book of Spirits (It's definitely in one of the books). Basically, a joy spirit (or anything similiar really) wants more joy. You may have noticed that humans don't walk around in a perpetual state of joy, and therein lies the basic conflict. The spirit pushes people to seek out joy to the exclusion of everything else; I think in the example the person ends up a drug addict, seeing as the easiest way to feel joy is to chemically induce it. Mind you, the spirit would probably be altered by the essence it's feeding on becoming a spirit of a particular kind of joy which makes it a bit more obviously problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T03:27:29-07:00","id":659185,"title":"","content":"I recall an example in one of the 1st ed books about a Joy/Happiness spirit feeding off the high of heroin addicts.<br /> <br /> The best way to emphasise the inhumane nature of spirits is to let them act in their animalistic logical manner while juxtaposing the very human context. A murder spirit encourages and feeds upon murder, be it out of geed, self-defense, patriotic duty (like a soldier) or mercy. It doesn't care, it just feeds on the Essence of purposeful sentient death. It's exact diet alters it's resonance and can turn it into a maggath if it varies it's feeding habits to rapidly.<br /> <br /> So if a Joy spirit attaches itself to a sadist, it will encourage the sadist to do things that make him happy. If it stays with him too long, it might begin to change but if it tries to switch to a different food source, it might need to inflict pain in order to feed on Joy, or else become maggath...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T04:01:41-07:00","id":659221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=659185#post659185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best way to emphasise the inhumane nature of spirits is to let them act in their animalistic logical manner while juxtaposing the very human context. A murder spirit encourages and feeds upon murder, be it out of geed, self-defense, patriotic duty (like a soldier) or mercy. <b>It doesn't care</b>, it just feeds on the Essence of purposeful sentient death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. Spirits do care about the flavor of the essence they consume, not merely because it defines them, but because it gives them specific focus. The joy spirit that is described in the example you mention developed a taste for essence linked to the joy of the high, of, initially, the buzz of underage alcohol consumption. You can, at the end of it's lifespan, mistake it for an spirit of addiction. Which is interesting because if you look at all the spirits you could encounter, they all likely get begotten by such a simple concept, and evolve into what they are as you present them.<br /> <br /> A spirit of &quot;murder for patriotic duty&quot; (soldiers will argue that killing for your country, in a conflict with defined rules of engagement isn't murder at all, but that's beyond the scope of this discussion) won't likely consider itself a mere spirit of murder, and it's a completely different beast from one born of revenge and sanity eclipsing passion.<br /> <br /> To expand on the example? The war spirit (&quot;murder for patriotic duty&quot;), maybe a reflection of the adrenaline from the survival in the battlefield will likely have bans against engaging &quot;friendlies&quot; (Your countrymen?). Rules, in essence.<br /> <br /> The Homicide-for-passion spirit? not so much. And you can already picture the war spirit hitching a ride back to the Estates with the soldier that spawned him, using it's influence to press enough stress to cause deadly fight or flight responses on the poor man, can't you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 09-10-2015, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:28:27-07:00","id":659877,"title":"","content":"Imagine Dolores Umbridge obsessing herself with making her students happy, obedient and smiling citizens... at any cost.<br /> <br /> Imagine a less moral version of Joy from<i> Upside Down</i> deciding that <b>her </b>Riley will be always happy no matter what... even if she must make some &quot;modifications&quot; in the girl\u00b4s mindscape:<br /> <i>&quot;Sadness. I\u00b4m afraid your services are no longer... required. Don\u00b4t worry, Anger, Fear, Disgust and me will take care of everything... providing <b>they </b>behave themselves&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 09-10-2015, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T19:38:06-07:00","id":660233,"title":"","content":"The idea of how 'good' spirits can cause bad things makes me think of an old Batman cartoon were someone found a way to take fear out of people, freeing them to take bold and beneficial action, only to be reminded that part of what keeps people from doing bad things is the fear of consequences. In the example of the joy spirit I would play up that under its influence people take actions that are self destructive (like drug addiction) without considering the consequences. I also think such a spirit would remain mobile, not anchoring itself to one person it would than have to spend influence on just to regain the essence thus spent. Imagine the horror of the girl who took actions while under the influence of joy, only to be left without any when the hammer falls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T03:38:19-07:00","id":660579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=660233#post660233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think such a spirit would remain mobile, not anchoring itself to one person it would than have to spend influence on just to regain the essence thus spent. Imagine the horror of the girl who took actions while under the influence of joy, only to be left without any when the hammer falls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? There's a misconception here. Spirits don't consume the emotion or thing they feed off when essence is generated from it. Even if the spirit left, the girl would get her high. The more the spirit uses it's influences, the more essence it would produce. Risking leaving one's territory is a less safer choice in the Darwinian hellscape that the shadow is, for the same reason we transitioned from nomadic to sedentary societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T05:19:58-07:00","id":660605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face#post659038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits. We all know that, from a human perspective, they're pretty much universally evil.</div> </div> </div> </div> The only spiritual beings in the WoD that are objectively evil as a whole are the Abyss critters, the Inferno, and Apep with a dash of Shaniatu.<br /> <br /> As for perverting things? Easy enough - you just take the negative aspects of something and focus on that. A child's playground isn't filled with happy spirits. Its filled with spirits of paranoia and watchfulness, as the stalkers keep tabs on kids, and parents fear their kids being kidnapped, but still go out because its what people do.<br /> <br /> Not every spirit needs to be evil. You just need to focus on those spirits that are naturally bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=660579#post660579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? There's a misconception here. Spirits don't consume the emotion or thing they feed off when essence is generated from it. Even if the spirit left, the girl would get her high. The more the spirit uses it's influences, the more essence it would produce. Risking leaving one's territory is a less safer choice in the Darwinian hellscape that the shadow is, for the same reason we transitioned from nomadic to sedentary societies.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, the whole drug-inducing-joy spirit is directly from one of the Werewolf books. A girl who gets accepted into college gets really excited and gives birth to a joy spirit. That spirit encouraged her into self-destructive behavior because her studies weren't producing joy. It urged her to indulge in drugs for the high. If not for the spirit, that girl never would have left her studies, but now she's on a self-destructive spiral because she was pushed that way. <br /> <br /> Mind you, the other spirits on college, especially the knoweldge spirits, should have couteracted the joy spirit and encouraged studying. And the joy spirit could have wandered off to a frat house or something. But it is an example from the books. Take it as you will<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-11-2015, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T05:27:51-07:00","id":660609,"title":"","content":"The Abyss specifically isn't evil, except when it is. It's just weird.<br /> <br /> From Dave Brookshaw, 'The Abyss doesn\u2019t have a morality (except when it does, as it is inherently contradictory) \u2014 it\u2019s a breakdown in reality. Abyssal intrusions poision the Fallen World around them as they interfere with the Fallen-Supernal duality. It can have beneficial effects, but they\u2019ll always come with a hefty side-serving of Zalgo.'<br /> <br /> Everyone's done a good job of pointing out that spirits are alien, not evil. I'll add that through Wounds, spirits can become infected. At this point they start acting maliciously and start trying to corrupt others maliciously as well, though aren't necessarily evil. <br /> <br /> From Chris Allen, 'So, Wounded spirits aren't 'bad' spirits. They're <i>corrupted</i>. Hatred, anger, death, murder, pain, anguish spirits are all perfectly normal spirits. The creatures that infest the pustules of taint that are Wounds have been infected and changed.'<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-11-2015, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T05:51:24-07:00","id":660612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=660605#post660605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the whole drug-inducing-joy spirit is directly from one of the Werewolf books. A girl who gets accepted into college gets really excited and gives birth to a joy spirit. That spirit encouraged her into self-destructive behavior because her studies weren't producing joy. It urged her to indulge in drugs for the high. If not for the spirit, that girl never would have left her studies, but now she's on a self-destructive spiral because she was pushed that way.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the other spirits on college, especially the knoweldge spirits, should have couteracted the joy spirit and encouraged studying. And the joy spirit could have wandered off to a frat house or something. But it is an example from the books. Take it as you will</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly are you trying to explain to me here? My point was in reply to <b>2ptTakrill </b>idea that the spirit should have wandered off. Nevermind that, no, the example is explicitly taken from the Book of Spirits (a Blue book, from the core line such as Antagonists, Armory, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T22:38:27-07:00","id":661509,"title":"","content":"I really don't get where the idea that spirits are stationary came from? Sure they have access to fetter numina that lock them to a person, place or thing, but there is an entire Shadow filled with spirits birthed by events in the real world. To use the drug girl example eventually that 'high' won't resemble joy in the least, more likely a desperate need to escape her despondent life. At that point the joy spirit either leaves her or drinking from her poisoned well changes it into something else, a mageth maybe. I think the spirit fettered to her would jump ship and fetter itself to something better, that produces more essence to its taste, at any time such an opportunity presents itself, and if there is already another joy spirit fettered to that target, one it would have to consume (or be consumed by) and thus grow stronger, well that is the nature of spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T22:40:42-07:00","id":661520,"title":"","content":"The exception to this would of course be the claimed, but in that case the spirit has tossed the girl out and is now using her flesh to hunt for outside sources of essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T22:57:02-07:00","id":661544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=661509#post661509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't get where the idea that spirits are stationary came from? Sure they have access to fetter numina that lock them to a person, place or thing, but there is an entire Shadow filled with spirits birthed by events in the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of those spirits are only active in areas of compatible resonance and have a relatively narrow range of awareness concerning where those areas are and what makes them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To use the drug girl example eventually that 'high' won't resemble joy in the least, more likely a desperate need to escape her despondent life. </div> </div> </div>Not all at once, which is part of the reason why non-desperate spirits still need watching.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At that point the joy spirit either leaves her or drinking from her poisoned well changes it into something else, a mageth maybe. </div> </div> </div>\u2026Explain what you think a magath is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T23:45:40-07:00","id":661612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=661544#post661544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of those spirits are only active in areas of compatible resonance and have a relatively narrow range of awareness concerning where those areas are and what makes them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether they're aware of what makes them is one of their difficulties, though I think it's overcome with rank and learning, but range is not a problem determining where those areas are.<br /> <br /> P184, 'Spirits can sense sources of Essence appropriate for their needs from up to a mile away, even across the Gauntlet without penalty. The \u201cSeek\u201d Numen (p. 193) increases this range.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face#post659038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what I was hoping to do was to open this topic and give people a place to swap ideas, or experiences, with making villains or terrifying encounters out of &quot;good spirits&quot;. I hope folks are willing to share.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many of the novels of Bentley Little are great examples of relatively benevolent spirits taking over, possibly being tainted by Wound spirits along the way and causing an overall thinning of the Gauntlet throughout the area the story takes place, most notably the Store. The Policy depicts what might be a man claimed by the spirit of an insurance company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Removed a wall of text about nomadic vs stationary spirits. 09-12-2015, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T00:38:43-07:00","id":661639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=661612#post661612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether they're aware of what makes them is one of their difficulties, though I think it's overcome with rank and learning, but range is not a problem determining where those areas are.<br /> <br /> P184, 'Spirits can sense sources of Essence appropriate for their needs from up to a mile away, even across the Gauntlet without penalty. The \u201cSeek\u201d Numen (p. 193) increases this range.'</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually not what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> &quot;The idea that spirits are stationary&quot; comes from the fact that Resonant Conditions that aren't stable, discrete objects are nonetheless part of a potential territory for the spirit, and it's generally easier for a spirit to build on established resonance if they have access to it than to go haring after a fresh source that might fade or be claimed by the time they arrive. The joy-spirit has access to the lingering joy-resonant Essence in the vicinity of the girl or her room or her house, and is only peripherally aware of other sources of Joy and it might lose its known cache if it goes to investigate more closely<br /> <br /> Neither innate awareness nor the Seek Numen tell the spirit how much Essence is present or the state of Shadow ecology in the area, which are fantastic reasons for a Gaffling to stick to the safer known food source. On the other end of the spectrum, stronger spirits generally tend to become sedentary because Essence tithes are a thing and personal refinement becomes a more focused concern at higher Rank. Spirits, as ephemeral beings, are creatures of pattern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T02:22:59-07:00","id":661683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=661639#post661639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually not what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> &quot;The idea that spirits are stationary&quot; comes from the fact that Resonant Conditions that aren't stable, discrete objects are nonetheless part of a potential territory for the spirit, and it's generally easier for a spirit to build on established resonance if they have access to it than to go haring after a fresh source that might fade or be claimed by the time they arrive. The joy-spirit has access to the lingering joy-resonant Essence in the vicinity of the girl or her room or her house, and is only peripherally aware of other sources of Joy and it might lose its known cache if it goes to investigate more closely<br /> <br /> Neither innate awareness nor the Seek Numen tell the spirit how much Essence is present or the state of Shadow ecology in the area, which are fantastic reasons for a Gaffling to stick to the safer known food source. On the other end of the spectrum, stronger spirits generally tend to become sedentary because Essence tithes are a thing and personal refinement becomes a more focused concern at higher Rank. Spirits, as ephemeral beings, are creatures of pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you're saying but I don't think it's that simple. A joy spirit, any conceptual spirit but lets just keep it under rank 6, has almost the same risks in regards to hunting as they do to sitting still. Another joy spirit may eat them, the Essence may run out, <i>their </i>Essence may run out, dormancy beckons, making them even easier prey for more powerful and hungrier spirits. Safety in numbers isn't a valid argument when everyone else is a cannibal. They face the same dangers as they would traveling to a new source of resonant Essence.<br /> <br /> This is why conceptual spirits are often the most likely to travel across the Gauntlet. Without something solid across the Gauntlet to anchor themselves to they need to act.<br /> <br /> Of course they might decide to stay stationary, and some jump across and ride or claim people, but there are also spirits that travel. The Mockingbird and, arguably, the Colossus from Wolfsbane. The Dreameater, Rafixul, Spearfinger. All seek out new sources of Essence, whether manufactured or taken advantage of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T20:38:48-07:00","id":662612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=661509#post661509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't get where the idea that spirits are stationary came from?</div> </div> </div> </div>My statement is hardly a broad generalization. Some spirits will be nomadic, just like some people are. The smart ones that will get to age and get more Rank usually manage to build a power base, such as a girl and her girlfriends getting hooked into drugs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=661509#post661509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure they have access to fetter numina that lock them to a person, place or thing, but there is an entire Shadow filled with spirits birthed by events in the real world. To use the drug girl example eventually that 'high' won't resemble joy in the least, more likely a desperate need to escape her despondent life.</div> </div> </div> </div>You clearly haven't experienced drug induced euphoria or what is more commonly referred to as 'getting high'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T20:43:15-07:00","id":662613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=661683#post661683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand what you're saying but I don't think it's that simple. A joy spirit, any conceptual spirit but lets just keep it under rank 6, has almost the same risks in regards to hunting as they do to sitting still. Another joy spirit may eat them, the Essence may run out, <i>their </i>Essence may run out, dormancy beckons, making them even easier prey for more powerful and hungrier spirits. Safety in numbers isn't a valid argument when everyone else is a cannibal. They face the same dangers as they would traveling to a new source of resonant Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? That's the kind of thing Strengthen alleviates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T21:00:07-07:00","id":662639,"title":"","content":"I would argue that drug induced euphoria is drug induced euphoria, not joy, and would warp the spirit into something else with a whole new area of influence (which, as I understand it, is a mageth).<br /> Besides, the true horror of a spirit, even a normally beneficial one, is that is extends its influence indiscriminately. If getting stone is what gives you joy then it will quickly push you to overdose, or make you so desperate for your next high that you take actions that are definitely not benevolent in its pursuit. It also affects those around you, like that bully who's greatest joy comes from abusing those who are weaker than him, or the neighborhood pedophile, or the BTK killer, or what have you. Take the example of the soldier who comes home from war with a killing (I would argue predator/prey) spirit in tow. Not only is he now more likely to strike out with lethal intent but also anyone around him. When he's on the road everyone suffers road rage. Spirits by their inhuman nature take everything to one extreme and too much of anything quickly becomes bad. Balance, it's a good thing. \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T21:02:26-07:00","id":662640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662613#post662613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How? That's the kind of thing Strengthen alleviates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Say the joy is caused by a movie. Eventually the movie is going to end, the theater close, the people gone, weeks later a new movie is showing and the only Essence coming is that of boredom and fear. One Girl's Ecstasy had the benefit of being able to stay with the girl and was aiming to claim her, but not all conceptuals are so lucky.<br /> <br /> Besides, the argument that Strengthen could give a spirit enough Essence to feast on at its current location and thus not have to leave ignores the fact that if a sudden wellspring of weak but resonant Essence elsewhere pops up it could do the same there. And either place it could be eaten by a larger spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-13-2015, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T21:45:39-07:00","id":662660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662639#post662639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that drug induced euphoria is drug induced euphoria, not joy, and would warp the spirit into something else with a whole new area of influence (which, as I understand it, is a mageth).</div> </div> </div> </div>Your understanding of what a magath is is, as seems common for the term, incredibly overbroad.<br /> <br /> A magath is, per the lexicon, a hybrid, unnatural spirit, or, as earlier books worded it, a hybrid spirit without a choir \u2014 the most typical magath are combinations of spirits of entirely different types, most famously artificial and nature spirits, like the combination glass/swarm/pain spirit from BoS. A simple shift from one type of good-feeling to another is relatively insignificant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662640#post662640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say the joy is caused by a movie. Eventually the movie is going to end, the theater close, the people gone, weeks later a new movie is showing and the only Essence coming is that of boredom and fear. One Girl's Ecstasy had the benefit of being able to stay with the girl and was aiming to claim her, but not all conceptuals are so lucky.<br /> <br /> Besides, the argument that Strengthen could give a spirit enough Essence to feast on at its current location and thus not have to leave ignores the fact that if a sudden wellspring of weak but resonant Essence elsewhere pops up it could do the same there. And either place it could be eaten by a larger spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the bit on p71, resonance persists beyond the activity that typifies it.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;everyone's a cannibal&quot; doesn't change the fact that broods happen and that not every spirit's nature is incompatible with cooperation, particularly when wolfpack tactics are a valid means of bringing down more powerful spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T22:14:10-07:00","id":662683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662660#post662660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the bit on p71, resonance persists beyond the activity that typifies it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forever? Of course not. But if it lingers then their ability to sense resonant Essence flows is even more useful because it'll still be there if they travel to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, &quot;everyone's a cannibal&quot; doesn't change the fact that broods happen and that not every spirit's nature is incompatible with cooperation, particularly when wolfpack tactics are a valid means of bringing down more powerful spirits. </div> </div> </div>Which is more reason for powerful spirits to eat weaker spirits before they can gather enough to use wolfpack spirits.<br /> <br /> Whatever. We've done this before. You believe spirits never travel. I believe they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-13-2015, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T22:33:13-07:00","id":662693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662683#post662683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever. We've done this before. <b>You believe spirits never travel. I believe they do.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the fact that you've just overtly misrepresented my point about why a supportable notion of spiritual territoriality exists into an absolute unilateral statement about the behavior of one of the broadest categories of principal antagonists for a line whose entire first-edition contents I have read within recent memory, weird exceptions and all, is reason enough to stop the conversation, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-13-2015, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T00:32:22-07:00","id":662771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662639#post662639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that drug induced euphoria is drug induced euphoria, not joy,</div> </div> </div> </div>Semantics. Euphoria is euphoria, regardless of it's source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AGZiLMGdCE0&amp;feature=youtu.be&amp;t=44s\" data-code=\"AGZiLMGdCE0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/AGZiLMGdCE0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The source of what the spirit represents colors it, of course, but drug caused euphoria is close enough that it's a viable source of sustenance for it. Magaths are abominations because it's a spirit of a concept consuming essence completely alien to what it currently represents. For instance... Bees consuming lava. Or a car eating dogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T00:53:50-07:00","id":662785,"title":"","content":"Car spirits have been called out to eat dog spirits without necessarily going off concept, al well as other road-kill. Just saying...<br /> <br /> Can we just be clear that spirits are not nice and do not understand morality? People seem to be missing that. Regardless of what WE (as humans) feel, the spirits of NWoD are alien animals feeding off the energy produced by/channelled through the concept they believe they represent.<br /> <br /> On another note; the spirits 'infected' by wounds and the Maeljin are not wholly spirits anymore. They are Diaboli - spirits of the Hisil who have become/are becoming demons of the Inferno. They are the equivalent of an Awakened worshiping Abyssals. They are Infected with power from the Lower Realms. The Maeltinet are invaders, Bale Hounds their fifth column.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T03:22:49-07:00","id":662867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662785#post662785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Car spirits have been called out to eat dog spirits without necessarily going off concept, al well as other road-kill. Just saying...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a significant difference, in my opinion, between actually ingesting some spirit's essence then merely discorporating it.<br /> <br /> A car spirit's ban can very well be &quot;Must run over every stray when the opportunity for it arrives&quot;. Just like a lightning spirit's might as well be &quot;Never strike twice at the same place&quot;.<br /> <br /> A magath with both influence in Cars and Dogs would be a mad thing with a misplaced sense of canine loyalty, without a pack to call it's own, and a hunger for things to get under it's hood-mouth at high velocities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662785#post662785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we just be clear that spirits are not nice and do not understand morality? People seem to be missing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That statement is literally in the first reply to this thread, but if you need to stress it again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 09-13-2015, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T04:51:56-07:00","id":662970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662639#post662639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, the true horror of a spirit, even a normally beneficial one, is that is extends its influence indiscriminately. If getting stone is what gives you joy then it will quickly push you to overdose, or make you so desperate for your next high that you take actions that are definitely not benevolent in its pursuit.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, then it learns that killing the proverbial hen of golden, tasty, yummy essence means it has to compete with other spirits for their own kicks. It's possible, but it's a mistake. The Gauntlet isn't the only reason the world hasn't devolved into a mad, post apocalyptic wasteland with the death of Father Wolf.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of the quote &quot;The road to Hell is paved with good intentions&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662639#post662639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also affects those around you, like that bully who's greatest joy comes from abusing those who are weaker than him, or the neighborhood pedophile, or the BTK killer, or what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you're starting to get the nuances of essence. A spirit who loves to feed on sadistic assholes tendencies is another beast entirely than One Girl's Ecstasy (the addiction inducing joy spirit).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/659038-for-evil-wears-a-pleasant-face?p=662639#post662639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the example of the soldier who comes home from war with a killing (I would argue predator/prey) spirit in tow. Not only is he now more likely to strike out with lethal intent but also anyone around him. When he's on the road everyone suffers road rage. Spirits by their inhuman nature take everything to one extreme and too much of anything quickly becomes bad. Balance, it's a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You gotta remember that there's always a method to every spirit's madness, more easily recognizable the lower the spirit's rank is. What kind of killing spirit is he feeding? I doubt it's one who feeds off summary executions. Flavor is key in these things. Once you realize that, you can make a whole town's assortments of spirits divided by broods, descants and choirs and even if the two spirits have the same influence, they'll be completely different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 09-13-2015, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}